<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchAgent for the account-rotation actor (CTL-2145).

  Do not edit this file directly — tokens are substituted by
  install-account-rotation.sh.

  WHY THIS SHAPE. On 2026-08-21 the fleet's rotation/lane tooling was run by a
  `nohup`'d loop owned by whichever concierge session happened to be alive. When
  that session's job record was cleaned up, the loop survived as a blind zombie
  holding deleted inodes — it could not act and nothing could tell that it
  couldn't. ~75 minutes of fleet outage.

  So this agent is deliberately a StartInterval ONE-SHOT, and the two keys that
  are ABSENT are as load-bearing as the ones present:

    - NO KeepAlive. launchd spawns a fresh short-lived process every interval and
      that process exits. There is no long-lived thing to zombie. (KeepAlive is
      also what makes launchd reap a job's backgrounded children on exit unless
      AbandonProcessGroup is set — learning
      launchd-keepalive-reaps-respawned-children.md, CTL-1285 — a trap this shape
      simply never enters.)
    - NO AbandonProcessGroup. The actor spawns nothing that must outlive it.

  Its liveness is therefore not a pid to check but a cadence: the agent either
  ran this interval or it did not, and account-rotation.log says which.

  Instructions:
    Run: bash plugins/dev/scripts/install-account-rotation.sh
    (or it is called automatically by `catalyst-stack install-services`)

  Manual steps (if needed):
    1. Copy to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.coalesce.catalyst-account-rotation.plist
    2. Replace REPLACE_WITH_ABSOLUTE with the absolute path to the scripts dir
       (e.g. /Users/you/catalyst/plugin-source/plugins/dev/scripts)
    3. Replace REPLACE_HOME with your home directory (e.g. /Users/you)
    4. Replace REPLACE_START_INTERVAL with the interval in seconds (e.g. 300)
    5. Replace REPLACE_ROTATION_MODE with off|shadow|enforce
    6. Load:
         launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.coalesce.catalyst-account-rotation.plist
    7. Verify:
         launchctl list | grep account-rotation
         tail -f ~/catalyst/account-rotation.log

  To unload, pass the installer its uninstall flag (the word "uninstall" behind the
  usual two leading hyphens; `install-account-rotation.sh -h` prints it in full).
  It is spelled out that way rather than shown literally because XML forbids a
  double hyphen ANYWHERE inside a comment — plutil -lint accepts one, but strict
  parsers reject the whole file. Do not "fix" this back.

  For a one-shot test run (shadow mutates nothing):
    CATALYST_ACCOUNT_ROTATION=shadow bash REPLACE_WITH_ABSOLUTE/coord/account-rotation-watch.sh
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>ai.coalesce.catalyst-account-rotation</string>

  <!--
    The actor runs from the PRISTINE scripts clone, not from the materialized
    ~/catalyst/comms/coord copy. Both are real files, but only the pristine clone
    is guaranteed to carry coord/lib/rotation-window.sh, which the actor treats as
    FATAL-if-missing (a rolling-window circuit breaker that silently isn't there is
    worse than none). install-account-rotation.sh refuses to bake a path inside a
    linked worktree or a temp dir for the same reason the orphan-sweep installer
    does: that path can be deleted, and a LaunchAgent pointing at a deleted script
    exit-127s every interval in silence.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>REPLACE_WITH_ABSOLUTE/coord/account-rotation-watch.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>REPLACE_START_INTERVAL</integer>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <!--
    The rollout knob, shipped IN THE TEMPLATE so the setting survives a reinstall.

    This installer regenerates and replaces the plist on every routine
    `catalyst-stack install-services`, so a mode hand-edited into the installed
    plist would be silently reverted by the next install — a knob a routine
    reinstall resets is worse than no knob (the CTL-1531 lesson, same mechanism).

    install-account-rotation.sh resolves the value, in order:
      1. an explicit CATALYST_ACCOUNT_ROTATION in the installing environment
      2. .catalyst/config.json → catalyst.accountRotation.mode
      3. the value ALREADY PRESENT in the installed plist   ← preserves a hand-flip
      4. "shadow" (ADR-023 dark-by-default)
    Anything not in off|shadow|enforce falls back to shadow — never to enforce: a
    typo must not arm something that restarts the whole stack.
  -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>CATALYST_ACCOUNT_ROTATION</key>
    <string>REPLACE_ROTATION_MODE</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>REPLACE_HOME/catalyst/account-rotation.log</string>

  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>REPLACE_HOME/catalyst/account-rotation.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
